I would argue a few things. 

1. This means that the issuer needs to communicate to me, for me to clear my flag then reset it.
2. They/I would need to do this every time, for every issuer that has an authorized trustline.
3. I already gave permission/trust to the issuer through adding their trustline therefore this process is redundant.

reviewCommentsList.body:
If I were reading this code in the future, I think I'd find the changed comment on line 136 misplaced.  My inclination is to remove the change from line 136 and, instead, add something like this comment just in front of this `if`:
```
            // The original implementation of featureDisallowIncoming was
            // too restrictive.  If
            //   o fixDisallowIncomingV1 is enabled and
            //   o The trust line already exists
            // Then allow the TrustSet.
```
I think this is an improvement.  But it's only a suggestion.  Take it, modify it, or leave it as you will.
